<!--
  STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1, wave 1 — the eight-row stocked-pool bestiary's LIVE
  side: pawn race + PawnKindDef pairs, per the two-def law in
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/weeping_stones_stocked_pool_2026-09-24.md
  §2 ("a species that is both seen in the pool and netted from it is TWO
  defs — pawn on wildAnimals/pen, catch item on the table"). The catch-item
  half (FishBase-lineage) ships in RM_StockedPoolCatchItems.xml, same folder
  tree, sibling file.

  🔴 NOT WIRED to any biome's wildAnimals yet — WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1
  (the RM_WeepingStones BiomeDef itself) is still proposed/unclaimed, so
  there is no RM_-tier biome to patch these into. These defs are complete
  and load-safe standalone; the wiring patch is owed once that item lands
  (see this mod's About.xml).

  §6 ambush ban honored: predator is left UNSET (false) on every row.
  "Nasty and way too active" (owner ruling) is represented as elevated
  manhunter chances (a handling accident can turn ugly) and flavor tools,
  never as a hunting-AI predator that stalks the truce line — violence here
  lives in the HANDLING, per the spec's own law.

  Placeholder art only (marked, not a considered choice — precedent:
  RM_Gelatid, src/RimMandrake/GelatinousSlime/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Gelatid.xml):
  the four fish rows reuse vanilla Cobra's Snake body/texture retinted; the
  three beast rows reuse vanilla Tortoise's TurtleLike body/texture
  retinted. Real art for all eight rides the art queue as of this wave
  (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/weepingstones_<species>_{south,east,north}.json,
  filed 2026-09-24 after a done/_artsrc/registry sweep found nothing
  existing for any of the eight names).
-->
